<title>CHINA: Zhejiang Expressway posts 1st H1 results.</title>
<headline>Zhejiang Expressway posts 1st H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million yuan unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (yuan)		3.83</p>
<p>    Dividend (yuan)	 nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     26.05 gain</p>
<p>    Net			 125.23</p>
<p>    Turnover		  235.64</p>
<p>    Company name	    Zhejiang Expressway Co Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close	     N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Zhejiang Expressway, a toll road operator in China eastern province of Zhejiang, was listed on the Hong Kong Stock Exchange on May 15, 1997. It issued 1.25 billion H-shares in global flotation of shares.</p>
<p>The interim results has been prepared on the assumption that the structure of the group as of March 1, 1997 had been in existence throughout the six months ended June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>Four months ended June 30</p>
<p>    Shr (yuan)		3.05</p>
<p>    Dividend (yuan)	 nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     26.05 gain</p>
<p>    Net			 105.14</p>
<p>    Turnover		  167.55</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain representing interest income generated from subscription monies of surplus applications during the share offer period of the H shares.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
